<title>USA: Mohave unit 1 restarted after shutdown early Mon.</title>
<headline>Mohave unit 1 restarted after shutdown early Mon.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 790 megawatt (MW) unit 1 at the Mohave coal-fired power plant near Laughlin, Nevada, was restarted around 1400 PST after being shut earlier in the day, sources familiar with the plant's operations said Monday.</p>
<p>No explanation for the outage was immediately available.</p>
<p>Mohave's 790 MW unit 2 was said to be operating normally.</p>
<p>The plant is majority owned and operated by Edison International's Southern California Edison Co.</p>
<p>--D Beasley, Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
